a quiet place part 2 picks up right  where the first leaves off  with their farmhouse in ruins the  surviving habits head out into the wider  world discovering that not everyone is  taken to the apocalypse as gracefully as  they have  let's break down the ending of a quiet  place part 2.  writer director and star john krasinski  calls the quiet place films a love  letter to his children and when a quiet  place part 2 ends it's easy to see why  well the first movie is all about the  sacrifices parents make to keep their  children  safe the second seesy abbott kids step  up and become heroes  with both reagan and marcus managing to  defeat the death angel  in both cases the kids are protecting  the adults around them reversing the  roles of the previous film when they  needed their parents protection  both of their victories also show how  their experiences in the harsh  post-apocalyptic world have changed them  and not necessarily for  the better most importantly though these  are two moments of huge personal growth  for marcus who is somehow even more  anxious in a quiet place part 2 than he  was in the first movie  his killing of a death angel is when he  finally overcomes his fears and stands  up for himself  for reagan it marks the end of her quest  she's done her part to save the world  honoring her father's memory in the  process  the most important character in a quiet  place part 2 may be one who's already  dead  lee abbott played by krazynski  sacrificed himself in order to save his  family in the first movie and his legacy  looms large over the sequel  lee taught marcus the skills the boy  uses to survive the movie's climax  reagan embarked on her journey to find  the radio tower because she says  it's what lee would have done that's why  the opening flashback in a quiet place  part 2  is more than an excuse to give krazynski  some screen time sure it's fun to see  how everything started and the opening  invasion is full of exciting set pieces  it's not just fan service though lee is  central to both reagan and marcus's arcs  so having him appear in the beginning  makes the ending hit a lot harder  while the first movie showed that lee  could be obsessive and hard-headed his  portrayal in part two  is overwhelmingly positive he's a good  father a nice neighbor and a well-liked  member of the community  showing up late to a little league game  seems to be his only flaw in this case  that's okay this time reagan marcus and  evelyn are dealing with lee's memory  not the actual man it only makes sense  that we see an idealized version of him  too  lee is also central to the story of  emmett the abbott's former neighbor who  is holed up in the old steel mill  emin is everything that lee isn't  instead of sacrificing himself to save  his family  emmett watched his wife and children die  while the abbotts tried to make life on  the farm feel as normal as possible  emmett trades comfort for survival  lee sought out other survivors emmett  argues that anyone who's still  alive isn't to be trusted i don't know  why he came all the way up here  there's nothing left the contrast  between lee and emmett becomes even more  pronounced when emmett reluctantly  agrees to accompany reagan on her trip  to the radio tower essentially becoming  a surrogate father figure to the young  girl  despite his graff and at times paranoid  exterior emmett is a good man and the  journey changes him  he forges a real bond with reagan even  using the limited amount of sign  language he knows to protect her from  danger  once he and reagan reach the island  emmett discovers that much to his  surprise  good people can still thrive in this  world when the monster attacks emmett  pulls moves straight from lee's playbook  putting himself in harm's way to save  others  he draws the monster's attention away  from the community by driving the truck  and puts himself in harm's way to  protect reagan at the radio  station emmett will never take lee's  place but by the end of the film he's  beginning to follow his old friend's  example  and the world is better off for it a  quiet place part 2 expands on the world  of the first movie by explaining the  monster's origins  yes they're from space and also showing  how different communities have reacted  to the apocalypse beyond the avid's farm  it's such an inspired sequel the world  expands in this one  because they have to venture out for  krazynski who wrote the screenplay for a  quiet place part 2 on his own this  presents a conundrum despite the wide  open cornfields and airy feel of the  avid's homestead the first quiet place  movie really takes after films like  alien and john carpenter's the thing  which trapped their heroes in a confined  space with a deadly paranoia-inducing  monster  going outside the farm threatens to  upend that balance robbing the sequel of  everything that makes the franchise  special  krazynski's solution to this problem is  clever while the world gets larger in a  quiet place part 2  the action itself moves into  increasingly small spaces  the opening flashback consumes an entire  town the first steps in the abbott's  journey take them into the wilderness  from there they move to the steel mill  and then a small bunker inside  by the time marcus and evelyn reach the  movie's climax they're trapped in a  cramped vault  similarly reagan and emmett go from  upstate new york to a remote isolated  island and end up making their final  stand in a tiny radio station  in this way krazynski ratchets up the  claustrophobic tension that defined the  first movie even while broadening the  series's mythology at the same time  a quiet place part 2 plays on the  confined atmosphere of the first movie  in another way too  in part two all of the characters are  trapped sometimes literally marcus steps  on an actual bear trap emmett has a rope  tied around his neck restricting his  movement  reagan ends up cornered in an old train  an entire community is stuck on an  island with nowhere to run when a  monster attacks  baby abbott is kept in a box and marcus  locks himself in the vault under the  steel plant  but the characters are mentally trapped  too marcus is dominated by a sphere  emmett is haunted by his inability to  save his family reagan's sense of  obligation and the example set by her  father can't be escaped  evelyn isn't exactly shackled to her  family but as the one who ensures their  survival she's forced to undertake some  risky missions at least until the kids  prove they can protect themselves in  that light reagan's quest takes on a  different connotation  killing the monsters isn't the goal it's  a means to an end  reagan's real mission revolves around  freedom the freedom to live a normal  life and to escape the terror that's  plagued them since the alien attack  began a quiet place part 2 ends on an  image of hope  reagan's implant dangling from the radio  station microphone its disruptive signal  being broadcast to people all over  america's east coast  and yet while this is clearly supposed  to be a sign of positive things to come  a quiet place park 2 proves time and  again that safety is an illusion  and that's without taking into account  the problems with reagan's plan  are people really going to be listening  to the radio without headphones in a  world where sound attracts monsters  if not how will they ever realize that  the random screeching coming over the  airwaves is the key to their survival  these are real questions but to be fair  neither quiet place movie is perfect  when it comes to plot logic  while the quiet place part 2 greatly  expands our understanding of the  post-apocalyptic world there are a  number of questions that remain when the  credits begin  narratively it's probably for the best  that these movies don't delve into the  larger socio-political implications of  the invasion but there are still things  we want to know about our characters  that the film simply doesn't answer  mainly what do reagan and emmett do now  do they return to the steel plant and  reunite with the rest of the abbott  family or do they wait for evelyn marcus  and the baby to come to them  what is the state of the island  community now that it has been attacked  by a monster and many of its residents  are dead  will life continue there like it did  before or is that refuge gone  as mentioned before it's also not clear  exactly how reagan's plan is gonna pan  out either  it feels like there are a few more steps  that need to be taken before the  monsters are in real trouble  finally after two movies are we ever  going to learn that baby's name  if a quiet place part 2 performs well at  the box office a sequel seems almost  guaranteed  what's less obvious is whether or not  the abbots will return on top of the  husband and wife team at the head of the  series maybe being ready to move on  it kind of feels like the abbott's story  is over it's not clear how much room for  growth they have left  the alien invasion was a global event  though and there are plenty of other  locations where people are probably  still struggling to survive  what do things look like in different  climates or other countries  and what would this world look like  years down the line habits or no habits  the quiet place movies thrive on being  stories about everyday people  stick to that core and the franchise  could run for a very long time  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos  about your favorite movies and tv shows  are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

